  </ul>
  <p>You answer questions about your own products: how to use a file, what a version includes, whether a refund is possible. Gumroad gives your customers a way to reach you and gives you the tools to act on what they ask for. This article covers both.</p>
  <h3 id="your-support-email">Your support email</h3>
  <p>Your <b>support email</b> is the address your customers reach you at. It is listed on the receipt of every sale, and it is where replies to the emails you send through Gumroad go.</p>
  <p>To set it, open your <a href="https://gumroad.com/settings">Settings</a> page, find the <b>Support</b> section, enter the address in the <b>Email</b> field, and click <b>Update settings</b>.</p>
  <p>If you leave it blank, your customers' replies go to the email address on your account instead, the one you use to sign in.</p>
  <h3 id="product-specific-support-emails">Product-specific support emails</h3>
  <p>If different products should be handled by different inboxes, you can set an address per product. In the same <b>Support</b> section, click <b>Add a product specific email</b>, enter the address, and pick the products it should cover.</p>
  <p>A few things to know:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>One address can cover as many of your products as you like.</li>
    <li>A product can only belong to one address. Products already assigned to another address won't be offered in the product picker.</li>
    <li>Products you don't assign keep using your account-level support email.</li>
    <li>Click <b>Update settings</b> to save, the same as any other change on this page.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3 id="which-emails-use-which-address">Which emails use which address</h3>
  <p>Once a product has its own support email, Gumroad uses it in these places:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Receipts.</b> The receipt for an order shows the product's support email, as long as every product in that order shares the same one. If a customer buys several products with different addresses in one order, the receipt shows your account-level support email instead.</li>
    <li><b>Emails and posts about that product.</b> When you <a href="169-how-to-send-an-update">send an email</a> to the customers of a single product, or of a single version or tier, replies go to that product's support email. Emails sent to a wider audience, to your followers, to your affiliates, or to the customers of more than one product, use your account-level support email.</li>
    <li><b>Workflow emails.</b> A <a href="131-using-workflows-to-send-automated-updates">workflow</a> built for one product behaves the same way, so replies to its emails land in that product's inbox.</li>
    <li><b>Pre-order confirmations and file-ready notifications.</b> These are always about one product, so they use that product's address.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>In every case, if the product has no address of its own, Gumroad falls back to your account-level support email, and then to the email address on your account.</p>
  <h3 id="answering-questions-from-the-sales-dashboard">Answering questions from the sales dashboard</h3>
  <p>Most support requests are answered from the <a href="268-customer-dashboard">Sales dashboard</a>. Open a customer to see what they bought and act on it. From there you can:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Fix a mistyped email address, then resend the receipt.</li>
    <li>Resend a receipt, a past email, or a workflow email the customer missed. Posts and workflow emails can only be resent to customers who are still subscribed to your emails; if a customer has unsubscribed, receipts are the only emails you can resend to them.</li>
    <li>Move a customer to a different version or tier without charging or refunding them.</li>
    <li>Disable a <a href="76-license-keys">license key</a> or change its number of seats.</li>
    <li>Cancel a membership.</li>
    <li>Issue a full or partial refund.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If a customer says they never received an email from you, <a href="54-not-receiving-updates">this article</a> walks through the usual causes. For missing receipts specifically, see <a href="78-my-customer-did-not-receive-a-receipt">customers not receiving receipts</a>.</p>
  <h3 id="refunds-and-your-refund-policy">Refunds and your refund policy</h3>
  <p>Refunds are yours to decide and yours to issue. <a href="47-how-to-refund-a-customer">Issuing a refund</a> covers full refunds, partial refunds, and what happens to your balance and fees afterwards.</p>
  <p>You can also tell customers where you stand before they buy by setting a <a href="335-custom-refund-policy">custom refund policy</a> on a product, which is shown on the product page and at checkout. Clear terms up front are the cheapest support you will ever provide.</p>
  <h3 id="reviews-and-review-reminders">Reviews and review reminders</h3>
  <p>Customers can <a href="222-product-ratings-on-gumroad">rate and review</a> what they bought, and Gumroad sends each of them a one-time reminder asking them to do so. You can turn those reminders off for your whole account in the <b>Review reminders</b> section of your <a href="https://gumroad.com/settings">Settings</a> page.</p>
  <p>A review you disagree with is often a support request in disguise. Reaching out to the customer and solving the underlying problem tends to work better than hiding ratings, and refunding a customer removes their rating automatically.</p>
  <h3 id="difficult-customers">Difficult customers</h3>
  <p>If someone abuses your products or your patience, you have two tools, both covered in <a href="329-customer-moderation">Customer moderation</a>: you can block an email address from buying from you again, and you can revoke a customer's access to content they have already bought.</p>
  <h3 id="supporting-customers-in-a-community">Supporting customers in a community</h3>
  <p>For products where the same questions come up again and again, a <a href="347-gumroad-community">Gumroad Community</a> chat can carry a lot of your support load. Answers stay visible to everyone who bought the product, and customers often answer each other.</p>
  <h3 id="when-gumroad-support-helps-instead">When Gumroad support helps instead</h3>
  <p>Some questions belong to us rather than to you: failed payments, download problems, fraudulent purchases, and anything about a customer's Gumroad account. <a href="20-how-do-i-contact-gumroad">Contact Gumroad</a> has the full split of what we handle and what creators handle, so you can forward a customer to us when it is ours to fix. Our <a href="348-support-response-times">response times</a> are usually well under a day.</p>
